.TH SEQUOIA-POLICY-CONFIG-CHECK 1 "2026-10-15" "Sequoia 0.8.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sequoia-policy-config-check \- validate Sequoia cryptographic
policy configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sequoia-policy-config-check
.RB [ --dump ]
.RI [ config.toml ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate a TOML configuration for Sequoia's cryptographic policy.
With no file argument, check the default policy configuration.
A successful check produces no output unless
.B --dump
is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dump
Write a policy configuration template to standard output.
.TP
.I config.toml
Read and validate this configuration file instead of the default configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The configuration was read and validated successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An argument, file, or configuration error occurred.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sq (1)
